# AutoBuild-H5000M-Openwrt feed configuration - mainline OpenWrt.
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: scripts/feeds strips comments with s/#.+$// and then skips
# blank lines. A lone "#" with nothing after it is therefore NOT a comment to
# that parser and dies with "Syntax error in feeds.conf.default". Every comment
# line here must have text after the hash.
# Upstream source is openwrt/openwrt (branch main, i.e. SNAPSHOT). The official
# OpenWrt feed repositories publish their development branch as master, which
# is what openwrt/openwrt's own feeds.conf.default references - keep that so
# the feeds stay in lockstep with the tree we build.
# Since OpenWrt 25.12 the package manager is apk, not opkg; CONFIG_PACKAGE_*
# symbols are unchanged and nothing here is ImmortalWrt-specific.

src-git packages https://github.com/openwrt/packages.git;master
src-git luci https://github.com/openwrt/luci.git;master
src-git routing https://github.com/openwrt/routing.git;master
src-git telephony https://github.com/openwrt/telephony.git;master
src-git video https://github.com/openwrt/video.git;master
# NOTE FOR EDITORS: the video feed IS listed, deliberately, and this is the
# result of an experiment rather than an oversight.
# (Blank comment lines are illegal in this file - see the header. The facts
# below are one paragraph run together on purpose; do not "tidy" it.)
# It was removed to reduce Kconfig recursive-dependency pressure after upstream
# dropped the AUDIO_SUPPORT/DISPLAY_SUPPORT gate (da6323e5, de2f69bf, c375123b)
# and the cycle count jumped 26 -> 166.  The count turned out to be a red
# herring: the run that last built green had 26 cycles, the run with video
# removed had 14, and it was the LOWER one that dropped qmodem.
# So the feed is kept.  Do not remove it to lower the cycle count.

# NOTE FOR EDITORS: the wwand feed (ddimension/openwrt-repo) is deliberately
# KEPT as an unconditional line, and this is counter-intuitive enough to
# warrant an explanation, because every other comment in this file argues the
# opposite for OTHER feeds.  (Blank comment lines are illegal here too.)
# Read the qmodem history in this order before changing anything here:
#   a836634 + feeds: video=on,  wwand=on   -> 26 cycles, qmodem SURVIVED
#   a836634 + feeds: video=off, wwand=off  -> 14 cycles, qmodem DROPPED
#   a836634 + feeds: video=on,  wwand=off  -> 166 cycles, qmodem DROPPED
# Those three rows are the whole story.  The cycle count moves 26/14/166 and
# does not track the outcome at all.  What DOES track the outcome is wwand:
# every surviving combination has the wwand feed installed, and every dropped
# one does not.  The wwand feed is the only source of libubus-lua-async, and
# installing it is what stops Kconfig from dropping the qmodem closure.
# This contradicts the libubus-lua-async theory further down, so be plain
# about what is established and what is not:
#   MEASURED - wwand feed present correlates perfectly with qmodem surviving.
#   NOT MEASURED - the mechanism, and specifically whether libubus-lua-async
#                  is the operative package or whether it is any feed at all
#                  that changes how Kconfig resolves the loop.  A feed with a
#                  different unrelated package would test that, and has not
#                  been run.
#   KNOWN COST - installing an unused dialer (wwand, luci-app-wwand,
#                  luci-proto-wwand) into a QModem image.  It is dead weight
#                  and its packages are NOT emitted, so it should not reach
#                  the firmware image; verify that before shipping.
# So: do not "clean up" this line, and do not trust a lower cycle count as
# evidence that qmodem will survive.  Rebuild and check
# `Verified all emitted packages survived defconfig`.
src-git wwand https://github.com/ddimension/openwrt-repo.git;main
